 "description": "One decisive fit of the wild type with its three mutants (description, discarded seeds).\n\nThe 60-generation screen (`fit_mutants.py`: population 24, 64 animals, each mutant one family of\nnine) traded the mutants against the wild type: tph-1 passed at its start and was lost, tax-4 passed\nat generations 20-40 and was lost. This fit asks whether that trade-off is the search's budget or\nthe model's limit.\n\n- The model and bounds: `fit_mutants.py`'s (the inhibitory scale at least 0.09; PDF's and ser-5's\n  strengths excitatory, after PDFR-1's Galpha-s and SER-5's Galpha-q couplings).\n- The start: the screen's last answer (generation 60, D 2.48).\n- The objective: v4's ranking score on the six families plus tph-1's, pdfr-1's and tax-4's two\n  lawn differences, each on its 200-animal band against its wild type on the same animals, the\n  mutants weighted to half the objective: 1,000 x undefined + sqrt((6\u00b7Dc^2 + 2\u00b7sum of the mutants'\n  terms^2) / 12), each mutant's term the root mean square of 10\u00b7asinh(z/10). Both guards apply.\n- The search: sep-CMA at population 48, sigma0 0.05, 200 animals a candidate, a cap of 150\n  generations on 16 workers, saved every generation and resumable.\n\nReadouts every 10 generations on the search's mean, on 200 animals (772,000,000 + i). Stop rules,\nfixed before the run and timed after the transient:\n\n1. at generation 50, stop if the readout D is more than 1 above its generation-0 readout;\n2. at generation 100, stop if neither tph-1 nor tax-4 has passed at any readout from 60 to 100.\n\nThe verdict, fixed before the run: at the end, the last answer is graded on two populations, the\nreadout one and a confirmation one (773,000,000 + i). If in both the wild type passes at least four\nfamilies and tph-1 and tax-4 both pass, W is designed around fits of the wild type with its mutants.\nOtherwise the limit is accepted for this model class.\n\nSeeds: fit animals 770,000,000 + 200\u00b7k + i; CMA 9487. Run from the repository root.\n",
